  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Find the average value of the function at point c</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Find the average value of the function \(f(x)={@quest_expr1@}\) over the interval \([{@a@},{@b2@}]\) and find the value of \(c\) that satisfies the Mean Value Theorem for f(x) in the given interval. </p>
<p>Average value \(=f(c)=\) [[input:ans1a]] [[validation:ans1a]][[feedback:prt1a]]</p></p>
<p>\(c=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Finding the average value of the function \(\displaystyle f(x)={@quest_expr1@}\) over the interval \([{@a@},{@b2@}]\) and finding \(c\) such that \(f(c)\) equals the average value of the function over \([{@a@},{@b2@}]\).</p>
<p>We use the formula \(f(c)=\displaystyle \frac{1}{b-a}\int_a^b f(x)dx\)</p>
<p>Applying this formula to \(\displaystyle f(x)={@quest_expr1@}\) over the interval \([{@a@},{@b2@}]\) </p>
<p>we have \(\displaystyle \frac{1}{{@b2@}-{@a@}}\displaystyle \int _{@a@}^{@b2@} {@quest_expr1@}\,dx\)</p>
<p>\( \begin{align}
\displaystyle \frac{1}{{@b2@}-{@a@}}\displaystyle \int _{@a@}^{@b2@} {@quest_expr1@}\,dx&=\frac{1}{{@b2-a@}} \times \left [  {@solution1@} \right ]_{@a@}^{@b2@}\\
&={@sol2@}
\end {align}\)</p>
<p></p>
<p>Find  \(c\) by Substituting \(c\) in the question expression</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle f(c)={@sol2@}={@sol3@}\)</p>
<p>Therefore \(\displaystyle c={@ta1@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
